GCC decides whether the target uses ELF with a case statement whose non-ELF
arm includes `*-*-pe*`, meant to catch Windows PE (Portable Executable)
targets like arm-wince-pe.  Shell globs span dashes, so
`x86_64-pc-linux-` + `peios` satisfies it:

    $ case x86_64-pc-linux-peios in *-*-pe*) echo MATCHED;; esac
    MATCHED
    $ case x86_64-pc-linux-gnu    in *-*-pe*) echo MATCHED;; esac
    (no match)

GCC therefore concluded Peios is not an ELF platform and SILENTLY disabled
LTO: `lto1` and `liblto_plugin.so` were never built, only the `lto-wrapper`
shim, so `-flto` failed with "LTO support has not been enabled in this
configuration".  Nothing else in GCC consults this macro — configure.ac's LTO
gate is its only caller — so the blast radius is exactly LTO.

This is the second time this glob has caught the name; config-sub-peios.sh
already works around the same collision in config.sub's OS normalizer, where
`pe*` mis-normalizes peios to obj=peios, os=''.  No vendor field escapes it
(`unknown`, `pc` and `peios` were all checked) -- the name collides, not the
triplet shape.

Claiming peios as ELF before the non-ELF list is reached is the minimal fix
and cannot affect any other target.  Tightening `*-*-pe*` itself would be the
upstream-shaped change, but risks real PE targets, so it is left alone.

Applied to config/elf.m4 (where upstream would take it) AND to the generated
`configure` (where it actually runs).  GCC's configure is generated by
autoconf 2.69 exactly; Peios ships 2.73, so the tree cannot be regenerated --
the same situation as gmp's C23 probe patch.

--- a/config/elf.m4	2026-08-11 23:25:57.718776157 +0100
+++ b/config/elf.m4	2026-08-11 23:25:57.748186845 +0100
@@ -15,6 +15,9 @@
 
 target_elf=no
 case $target in
+  *-linux-peios*)
+    target_elf=yes
+    ;;
   *-darwin* | *-aix* | *-cygwin* | *-mingw* | *-aout* | *-*coff* | \
   *-msdosdjgpp* | *-vms* | *-wince* | *-*-pe* | \
   alpha*-dec-osf* | *-interix* | hppa[[12]]*-*-hpux* | \
--- a/configure	2026-08-11 23:25:57.725678875 +0100
+++ b/configure	2026-08-11 23:25:57.749679005 +0100
@@ -9729,6 +9729,9 @@
 
 target_elf=no
 case $target in
+  *-linux-peios*)
+    target_elf=yes
+    ;;
   *-darwin* | *-aix* | *-cygwin* | *-mingw* | *-aout* | *-*coff* | \
   *-msdosdjgpp* | *-vms* | *-wince* | *-*-pe* | \
   alpha*-dec-osf* | *-interix* | hppa[12]*-*-hpux* | \
